[claims]

## Overview
#c1[overview,i5] Kilo is a lightweight text editor that requires a single filename argument, reading the file or opening a new buffer without external dependencies.
  > README.md:4 #292daf6ba680
  > README.md:8 #4c6b68363986
  > README.md:16-17 #efb6b4eb18e1
  > kilo.c::editorOpen #a74a759a7b82
  > kilo.c::main #846ece275c31
#c2[overview,i5] The core event loop continuously renders the interface with editorRefreshScreen and processes user input via editorProcessKeypress.
  > kilo.c::main #846ece275c31
#c3[overview,i5] Terminal raw mode and editorReadKey interpret raw input and multi-byte VT100 escape sequences into distinct editor actions and navigation keys.
  > README.md:16-17 #efb6b4eb18e1
  > kilo.c::enableRawMode #cd72cf1e3c04
  > kilo.c::editorReadKey #1235ba3b05b0
#c4[overview,i5] Screen rendering aggregates row text and status bars into a single write buffer, reserving space for the status message display.
  > kilo.c:888-889 #bcf56b296256
  > kilo.c:976-978 #7130e51edcd1
  > kilo.c::updateWindowSize #6516dd852835
#c5[overview,i5] Window resize events handled via SIGWINCH update terminal dimensions, clamp cursor positions, and immediately refresh the screen.
  > kilo.c::updateWindowSize #6516dd852835
  > kilo.c::handleSigWinCh #9b64b04397af
  > kilo.c::initEditor #880014f10916
#c6[overview,i5] Row modifications insert characters or rows, adjust dirty state tracking, and recursively update syntax highlighting across multiline structures.
  > kilo.c:513-516 #24cbbc4d8c9d
  > kilo.c::editorInsertRow #ee0d5fc82d49
  > kilo.c::editorRowInsertChar #d6c3990144bd
#c7[overview,i5] Keybindings support saving, searching with dynamic syntax highlighting, and quitting, which requires multiple confirmations if unsaved changes exist.
  > README.md:12-14 #af9f24d591ea
  > kilo.c:1022-1028 #19d8a36dbf23
  > kilo.c::editorProcessKeypress #1164e28a1a02
#c8[overview,i5] Syntax highlighting patterns are matched against filenames, updating and highlighting row contents during editing and searches.
  > kilo.c:513-516 #24cbbc4d8c9d
  > kilo.c::editorSelectSyntaxHighlight #9dc867cf550c
  > kilo.c:1022-1028 #19d8a36dbf23

## (root)
#c9[i5] Kilo is a small text editor implemented in fewer than 1,000 lines of code as measured by cloc.
  > README.md:4 #292daf6ba680
#c10[i3] Kilo is run from the command line using the syntax kilo <filename>.
  > README.md:8 #4c6b68363986
#c11[i4] Keybindings in Kilo include CTRL-S to save, CTRL-Q to quit, and CTRL-F to find a string.
  > README.md:12-14 #af9f24d591ea
#c12[i5] Kilo does not depend on any external library, not even curses, and relies on standard VT100 escape sequences.
  > README.md:16-17 #efb6b4eb18e1
#c13[i3] Kilo is in alpha stage and incorporates code from the author's previous projects, load81 and linenoise.
  > README.md:17-19 #0c5274601a06
#c14[i4] Salvatore Sanfilippo (antirez) wrote Kilo and released it under the BSD 2-clause license.
  > README.md:25-26 #1738738f099b
#c15[i3] Terminal raw mode sets a 100 ms read timeout with zero minimum return bytes using VMIN = 0 and VTIME = 1.
  > kilo.c::enableRawMode #cd72cf1e3c04
#c16[i4] editorReadKey parses multi-byte VT100 escape sequences, mapping them into KEY_ACTION enum values such as arrow keys, page controls, DEL_KEY, HOME_KEY, and END_KEY.
  > kilo.c::editorReadKey #1235ba3b05b0
#c17[i4] editorUpdateSyntax recursively propagates syntax highlighting updates to following rows if a row's multiline open comment state changes.
  > kilo.c:513-516 #24cbbc4d8c9d
#c18[i3] editorSelectSyntaxHighlight requires patterns starting with a period to match the end of the filename, whereas other patterns can match anywhere.
  > kilo.c::editorSelectSyntaxHighlight #9dc867cf550c
#c19[i4] editorInsertRow inserts an erow at index 'at', shifts subsequent rows, updates their idx fields, and increments E.numrows and E.dirty.
  > kilo.c::editorInsertRow #ee0d5fc82d49
#c20[i3] editorRowInsertChar pads the row with space characters up to the target index if 'at' is greater than row->size.
  > kilo.c::editorRowInsertChar #d6c3990144bd
#c21[i3] editorOpen exits the program immediately if fopen fails with any errno other than ENOENT.
  > kilo.c::editorOpen #a74a759a7b82
#c22[i4] editorRefreshScreen hides the cursor, positions it at home, renders lines and status into an abuf, and sends it in a single write call.
  > kilo.c:888-889 #bcf56b296256
#c23[i3] The second status bar row only shows E.statusmsg if the message is set and less than 5 seconds have elapsed since E.statusmsg_time.
  > kilo.c:976-978 #7130e51edcd1
#c24[i4] editorFind searches match substrings in row render buffers, temporarily highlights matches with HL_MATCH, and restores original syntax highlighting upon navigation or exit.
  > kilo.c:1022-1028 #19d8a36dbf23
#c25[i4] When the editor buffer is modified, Ctrl-Q requires 3 consecutive presses to exit, resetting the counter on any other keypress.
  > kilo.c::editorProcessKeypress #1164e28a1a02
#c26[i2] The editor explicitly ignores Ctrl-C keypresses to prevent accidental loss of unsaved changes.
  > kilo.c::editorProcessKeypress #1164e28a1a02
#c27[i4] updateWindowSize subtracts 2 from E.screenrows to reserve room for the status bar after querying the terminal dimensions.
  > kilo.c::updateWindowSize #6516dd852835
#c28[i3] If getWindowSize fails inside updateWindowSize, the program prints a perror message and exits with status 1.
  > kilo.c::updateWindowSize #6516dd852835
#c29[i4] The SIGWINCH signal handler updates the window size, clamps E.cy and E.cx within the new screen boundaries, and refreshes the screen.
  > kilo.c::handleSigWinCh #9b64b04397af
#c30[i4] initEditor zeroes cursor and offset states, updates window dimensions, and registers handleSigWinCh for SIGWINCH.
  > kilo.c::initEditor #880014f10916
#c31[i3] kilo requires exactly one argument for the filename, otherwise it prints usage instructions to stderr and exits with status 1.
  > kilo.c::main #846ece275c31
#c32[i5] The main event loop continuously calls editorRefreshScreen followed by editorProcessKeypress on STDIN_FILENO.
  > kilo.c::main #846ece275c31

[probes]
?p1 Which tool was used to verify that Kilo has less than 1K lines of code?
  = cloc
  > README.md:4 #292daf6ba680
?p2 What errno value is set if enableRawMode is called on a file descriptor where isatty returns false?
  = ENOTTY
  > kilo.c::enableRawMode #cd72cf1e3c04
?p3 What heap pointers are freed when editorFreeRow is called on an erow?
  = row->render, row->chars, and row->hl.
  > kilo.c::editorFreeRow #001586e3311a
?p4 What macro defines the number of times Ctrl-Q must be pressed to quit when the file is dirty?
  = KILO_QUIT_TIMES (set to 3)
  > kilo.c:1187 #bddc20b86e60
?p5 What terminal escape sequence standard does Kilo utilize?
  = VT100
  > README.md:17 #ce6f8d037e58
?p6 What escape sequence is transmitted by getCursorPosition to query the terminal's cursor location?
  = \x1b[6n
  > kilo.c::getCursorPosition #b704af9a9c92
?p7 What delimiter separates each row in the buffer allocated by editorRowsToString?
  = A newline character ('\n').
  > kilo.c::editorRowsToString #b6f50327574f
?p8 What does editorProcessKeypress do upon receiving a CTRL_C keypress?
  = It ignores the keypress and does nothing.
  > kilo.c::editorProcessKeypress #1164e28a1a02
?p9 From which two projects did the author take code to write Kilo?
  = load81 and linenoise
  > README.md:18-19 #21ed19e0bfb9
?p10 Which terminal color code is returned by editorSyntaxToColor for HL_KEYWORD1?
  = 33 (yellow)
  > kilo.c::editorSyntaxToColor #819747c749b1
?p11 What occurs in editorDelChar when invoked at column 0 of a line past row 0?
  = It appends the current row's text to the previous row and deletes the current row via editorDelRow.
  > kilo.c::editorDelChar #9311d4da2443
?p12 Which keys trigger editorDelChar in editorProcessKeypress?
  = BACKSPACE, CTRL_H, and DEL_KEY.
  > kilo.c::editorProcessKeypress #1164e28a1a02
?p13 Under which license is Kilo released?
  = BSD 2 clause license
  > README.md:26 #fe6c5ed874ed
?p14 Which terminal color code is assigned to HL_MATCH in editorSyntaxToColor?
  = 34 (blu)
  > kilo.c::editorSyntaxToColor #819747c749b1
?p15 What permissions mask does editorSave pass to open() when creating or opening E.filename?
  = 0644
  > kilo.c::editorSave #a9e9709084c7
?p16 How many rows does updateWindowSize subtract from E.screenrows to make room for the status bar?
  = 2
  > kilo.c::updateWindowSize #6516dd852835
?p17 What key combination is used to find a string in Kilo?
  = CTRL-F
  > README.md:14 #a0280e8f56cc
?p18 What characters define single-line and multi-line comments in the default C/C++ syntax configuration?
  = "//" for single-line, "/*" and "*/" for multi-line
  > kilo.c:193 #5493921d29cd
?p19 When does editorRefreshScreen display the centered welcome message?
  = When E.numrows is 0 and the current row index y equals E.screenrows/3.
  > kilo.c:894 #a20d11c728f9
?p20 Which signal is caught by handleSigWinCh?
  = SIGWINCH
  > kilo.c::initEditor #880014f10916
?p21 What action does editorReadKey take if the read system call returns -1?
  = It calls exit(1).
  > kilo.c::editorReadKey #1235ba3b05b0
?p22 What character representation is displayed when an editor character has highlight type HL_NONPRINT and its value is 26 or less?
  = '@' plus the character's value.
  > kilo.c:924-925 #c14df5fcfc38
?p23 What is the initial status message set in main?
  = "HELP: Ctrl-S = save | Ctrl-Q = quit | Ctrl-F = find"
  > kilo.c::main #846ece275c31
?p24 How are tabs rendered by editorUpdateRow into row->render?
  = As spaces aligning up to the next multiple-of-8 boundary.
  > kilo.c::editorUpdateRow #298eb05dee6b
?p25 What is the maximum query length supported by editorFind?
  = 256
  > kilo.c:1012 #f8ea1756a445
?p26 What does editorFileWasModified return?
  = E.dirty
  > kilo.c::editorFileWasModified #f0e785df3c1d
?p27 If pressing ESC in editorFind exits the search, what coordinates and offsets are restored?
  = E.cx, E.cy, E.coloff, and E.rowoff are restored to their saved values.
  > kilo.c:1044-1047 #d9b7d964c0d6
